      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much deck stripper do I need for a 300 square foot deck?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Three hundred square feet is usually the floor only. Add roughly 3 square feet per linear foot of railing, 2 per step per foot of width, and the fascia, which typically brings the real treated surface closer to 480. On a worn semi-transparent stain that is about 2.5 gallons of working solution; on one coat of solid stain, about 6."
