        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many square feet does a gallon of deck stripper cover?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Between 100 and 200 square feet per application, but plan from the effective rate that includes the number of applications you will actually need. That is roughly 185 for a worn semi-transparent stain, 80 for one coat of solid stain, and 45 for deck paint over two rounds."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need to measure the railings separately?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, and it is the most commonly skipped step. A railing has two faces of top and bottom rail, the posts, and four faces on every spindle. Allow about 3 square feet per linear foot as a shortcut, or 4 for a stair railing. On a typical deck this adds a third or more to the floor area."
          }
