        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measure the whole surface, not the floor. Add about 3 square feet per linear foot of railing, 4 for stair railing, 2 per step per foot of width, and the fascia. On a typical deck that is 40 percent more surface than the floor area everyone quotes, and it is the single biggest reason people run short.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then pick your coverage figure from the finish you actually have rather than the front of the bottle: roughly 185 effective square feet per gallon for a worn semi-transparent stain, 80 for one coat of solid, and 45 for paint across two applications. Add fifteen percent, and buy the brightener at the same time, because after a caustic strip it is part of the job rather than an extra.
          </p>
        </div>

